Slide 2: What are Custom Agents?
Speaker Note: Think of a Custom Agent as a specialized assistant with a persistent persona, domain expertise, and specific tool access
. Unlike a standard chat session, these agents are configured to adopt a role—like a Security Reviewer or a Planner—shaping how the AI thinks and communicates throughout the entire session
.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Slide 3: The Customization Hierarchy
Speaker Note: It’s easy to get confused by all the new terms, so let's look at the hierarchy.
Instructions are "always-on" rules for the whole team
.
Prompts are manual, repeatable slash commands
.
Skills are reusable, multi-step workflows
.
Custom Agents (formerly known as Chat Modes) provide role and tool boundaries
. You pick them when you need a specific specialist for a specific job
.

