Slide 4: Anatomy of .agent.md
Speaker Note: Every agent is defined by a simple Markdown file ending in .agent.md
. It has two parts:
YAML Frontmatter: This is the "brain" configuration where you name the agent, choose the AI model, and list available tools like codebase or terminal
.
Markdown Body: This is the "persona" instructions where you define the working style and specific expertise using #tool: syntax to reference capabilities
.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Slide 5: Storage and Selection
Speaker Note: Where do these live? For team-wide access, place them in the .github/agents folder of your repository
. For personal use across all projects, use ~/.copilot/agents
. Once they're in the right folder, they appear automatically in the Agent Picker in VS Code, or you can invoke them directly by @mentioning their name
.

