Slide 9: Professional Best Practices
Speaker Note: To make these agents effective, follow three rules:
The 4x6 Rule: Keep your instructions concise—no more than 4-6 lines/words per core concept
.
Code Over Theory: One real code example in your instructions is better than three paragraphs of text
.
Strict Boundaries: Clearly define "Always/Never" rules
. For example: "Never modify production configs" or "Always check for unused variables"
.

