Slide Content: Synthesis: The Ultimate Copilot Stack
Visual Recommendation: A layered "Stack" diagram where Hooks sit at the bottom (enforcement), Instructions form the foundation (behavior), and MCP acts as the bridge to the side (connectivity)
.
Layer 1: The Behavior Layer (Instructions)
Always-on standards for the entire workspace or organization
.
Layer 2: The Persona & Boundary Layer (Custom Agents)
Persistent specialists (Planning, Security, Implementation) with defined tool limits
.
Layer 3: The Task & Workflow Layer (Prompts & Skills)
On-demand actions and multi-step runbooks like /security-review or /scaffold-module
.
Layer 4: The Connectivity Layer (MCP)
Live access to external systems like GitHub Issues, Jira, or cloud metadata
.
Layer 5: The Policy Enforcement Layer (Hooks)
Hard gates that approve or deny tool executions based on security rules
.

